stage: 3
finding: Medium — a runner signal does not cancel the selected integration loop. `bun /tmp/shallot-review-signal-probe.ts` interrupted the first of two rows and returned `exitCode:1`, but `laterRowStarted:true`; summary was `1 passed, 1 failed` and the report contained a passing second row. Thus SIGTERM can trigger new work after interruption. Medium — the `run()` fallback can preserve a false-green summary and invalid JUnit instead of using `failedJunit`: `bun /tmp/shallot-review-junit-probe.ts` returned exit 1 but printed `shallot test: 2 passed, 0 failed`; report was only `<?xml version="1.0"?><testsuites tests="2"><testsuite tests="2">`, and Python `xml.etree.ElementTree.parse` failed with `ParseError: no element found`. `readJunitSummary` accepts partial XML by regex, while `appendRunnerFailure` increments only attributes present and does not ensure an appended testcase or valid document.
